<%# Body copy lives in config/locales/ru.yml and en.yml under
    notification_mailer.welcome_letter.body -- see NotificationMailer for
    why the mail is rendered in the recipient's locale, not the sender's.

    @host (set by NotificationMailer#welcome_letter via #app_host) replaces
    the "bien.kg" that was hardcoded into the Merb-era version of this
    template: encounter-engine is meant to be installed by anyone on their
    own domain (see README.md), so naming one specific installation's
    domain in every deployment's mail was a bug, not a feature. Defaults to
    "bien.kg" so existing deployments see no change; override per-instance
    with APP_HOST, alongside this app's other per-instance ENV overrides
    (TZ, DEFAULT_LOCALE -- see config/application.rb). The subject uses the
    same @host, via #app_host and subject_vars, so ru/en subject and body
    always agree on which host they're naming. %>
<%= t("notification_mailer.welcome_letter.body",
      host: @host,
      email: @user.email,
      password: @password) %>
